1
00:00:07,707 --> 00:00:09,376
The test results are back!

2
00:00:12,412 --> 00:00:13,346
It's positive.

3
00:00:14,080 --> 00:00:15,482
No way!

4
00:00:15,548 --> 00:00:17,183
- Hurry!
- Right!

5
00:00:18,618 --> 00:00:20,653
Saturation under 90%!

6
00:00:20,720 --> 00:00:21,755
Michiko…

7
00:00:21,821 --> 00:00:23,623
- Demon!
- Dr. Daimon!

8
00:00:23,690 --> 00:00:25,158
Dr. Daimon, hang in there!

9
00:00:26,493 --> 00:00:27,394
Michiko!

10
00:00:29,796 --> 00:00:33,433
<i>This is the story</i>
<i>of a maverick woman doctor.</i>

11
00:00:36,836 --> 00:00:39,105
THREE MONTHS EARLIER

12
00:00:42,876 --> 00:00:46,379
MICHIKO DAIMON
FREELANCE SURGEON

13
00:00:55,455 --> 00:00:59,092
How cute! Very cute!

14
00:01:26,152 --> 00:01:29,289
KEI ICHIKI
RESPIRATORY SURGEON

15
00:01:30,290 --> 00:01:31,791
Dr. Daimon!

16
00:01:31,858 --> 00:01:33,460
What are you doing here?

17
00:01:39,165 --> 00:01:42,001
The deputy prime minister's
pulmonary embolism surgery

18
00:01:42,068 --> 00:01:43,436
is in two hours!

19
00:01:43,503 --> 00:01:44,504
You have to hurry!

20
00:01:44,571 --> 00:01:46,406
I still have two hours.

21
00:01:46,473 --> 00:01:48,308
- Want to feed them?
- No, thanks.

22
00:01:48,374 --> 00:01:49,209
It's fun.

23
00:01:49,275 --> 00:01:50,844
They're so cute!

24
00:02:11,664 --> 00:02:13,366
Excuse me.

25
00:02:13,933 --> 00:02:15,301
Woah!

26
00:02:19,806 --> 00:02:21,541
Get him away from that wiring!

27
00:02:21,608 --> 00:02:22,742
Don't touch him!

28
00:02:47,033 --> 00:02:50,470
This is bad. Cardiac arrest.
He's in V-fib.

29
00:02:59,345 --> 00:03:01,648
What will we do? There's no AED near here.

30
00:03:01,714 --> 00:03:03,216
- Call an ambulance!
- Right.

31
00:03:04,317 --> 00:03:06,686
Sorry. I've lost all my strength.

32
00:03:06,753 --> 00:03:08,121
You're hopeless, damn you!

33
00:03:08,188 --> 00:03:09,255
I'm sorry.

34
00:04:03,309 --> 00:04:04,944
NEW ZEALAND'S DEPUTY PRIME MINISTER

35
00:04:25,698 --> 00:04:26,766
Dr. Daimon!

36
00:04:27,433 --> 00:04:29,202
A message from the prime minister.

37
00:04:29,269 --> 00:04:30,103
What?

38
00:04:59,065 --> 00:05:01,934
That was really an amazing surgery.
I learned a lot.

39
00:05:02,735 --> 00:05:05,972
But that dropkick you did was a bit much.

40
00:05:06,039 --> 00:05:07,273
You're not Tarzan.

41
00:05:07,974 --> 00:05:09,108
It still hurts.

42
00:05:09,776 --> 00:05:12,545
You're a bigger wimp than a lamb.

43
00:05:15,415 --> 00:05:18,084
There's another call. It's from Tokyo.

44
00:05:20,586 --> 00:05:21,587
<i>Michiko!</i>

45
00:05:21,654 --> 00:05:23,456
<i>At last, I've found you.</i>

46
00:05:23,956 --> 00:05:25,191
<i>I looked all over for you!</i>

47
00:05:25,258 --> 00:05:28,661
Akira! Ben Casey! Long time no see.

48
00:05:28,728 --> 00:05:32,565
Don't act so casual!
I was worried about you.

49
00:05:32,632 --> 00:05:35,234
I really thought you were in New York.

50
00:05:35,301 --> 00:05:36,936
But you're in New Zealand?

51
00:05:37,003 --> 00:05:38,638
You should come, too, Akira.

52
00:05:38,705 --> 00:05:40,673
Quit joking around.

53
00:05:40,740 --> 00:05:42,542
Get back here right now.

54
00:05:42,608 --> 00:05:45,445
There's hardly any surgeries due to COVID.

55
00:05:45,511 --> 00:05:49,315
My Doctor Referral Agency
has gone deep into the red.

56
00:05:51,217 --> 00:05:55,822
We need Michiko to make us
some money. Right, Ben Casey?

57
00:05:57,323 --> 00:06:00,360
BEN CASEY

58
00:06:00,426 --> 00:06:02,462
<i>2021.</i>

59
00:06:02,995 --> 00:06:06,265
<i>The ravages</i>
<i>of a once-in-a-century pandemic</i>

60
00:06:06,332 --> 00:06:09,135
<i>have devastated</i>
<i>the world's medical systems.</i>

61
00:06:09,702 --> 00:06:11,537
<i>Meanwhile, with the prodigious might</i>

62
00:06:11,604 --> 00:06:14,207
<i>of a cornered animal,</i>
<i>Japan's medical universities</i>

63
00:06:14,273 --> 00:06:16,676
<i>have firmly withstood the storm.</i>

64
00:06:16,743 --> 00:06:17,643
Oh, wow.

65
00:06:17,710 --> 00:06:21,447
Our hospital is completely under
the control of Internal Medicine.

66
00:06:23,116 --> 00:06:25,651
It has been a while.
I feel so out of place here now.

67
00:06:27,720 --> 00:06:29,489
Director of Surgery Ebina.

68
00:06:30,456 --> 00:06:31,657
Yes?

69
00:06:31,724 --> 00:06:33,126
Don't be so pathetic.

70
00:06:33,793 --> 00:06:35,261
Yes, sir. Sorry.

71
00:06:37,630 --> 00:06:39,532
They're here.
Branch Director, they're here.

72
00:06:53,012 --> 00:06:55,581
Well…
Director of Internal Medicine Hachisuka.

73
00:06:55,648 --> 00:06:58,718
I thought an armored riot squad
had burst in.

74
00:07:01,454 --> 00:07:03,589
Branch Director Hiruma.

75
00:07:03,656 --> 00:07:08,194
Branch Director Hiruma, that seat
belongs to this hospital's leader,

76
00:07:08,261 --> 00:07:10,463
Director of Internal Medicine Hachisuka.

77
00:07:11,464 --> 00:07:12,465
Listen here.

78
00:07:13,466 --> 00:07:16,235
Even before you became a doctor,

79
00:07:16,302 --> 00:07:19,906
this has always been my place.

80
00:07:19,972 --> 00:07:22,542
Only because we're in a crisis now,

81
00:07:22,608 --> 00:07:25,845
this hospital has been put under
the control of Internal Medicine.

82
00:07:26,646 --> 00:07:29,048
But it's only a temporary situation.

83
00:07:29,115 --> 00:07:33,119
I brought everyone
in the Surgery Department here

84
00:07:33,186 --> 00:07:36,055
from the branch hospital

85
00:07:36,122 --> 00:07:39,192
to discuss what to do
after the pandemic is under control.

86
00:07:39,258 --> 00:07:40,226
Right!

87
00:07:41,327 --> 00:07:42,361
You're spraying!

88
00:07:42,428 --> 00:07:45,731
Microdroplets can fly
more than two meters!

89
00:07:45,798 --> 00:07:47,166
Please don't shout.

90
00:07:47,233 --> 00:07:50,603
Transmission prevention measures
by the surgeons are too lax.

91
00:07:50,670 --> 00:07:52,338
How can you say that?

92
00:07:52,405 --> 00:07:54,440
Besides being vaccinated twice,

93
00:07:54,507 --> 00:07:56,476
we're scrupulously careful!

94
00:07:56,542 --> 00:07:58,144
Director of Surgery Ebina,

95
00:07:58,211 --> 00:08:02,081
as head of Surgery,
you need to protest as well.

96
00:08:02,148 --> 00:08:03,216
Yes, sir.

97
00:08:04,283 --> 00:08:05,117
Listen.

98
00:08:05,184 --> 00:08:06,853
When we surgeons perform surgery,

99
00:08:06,919 --> 00:08:09,622
it's way more stressful
than internists' work.

100
00:08:09,689 --> 00:08:10,990
It's exhausting!

101
00:08:11,491 --> 00:08:14,894
You internists don't have the right
to complain about us!

102
00:08:16,128 --> 00:08:17,129
Oh, sorry.

103
00:08:18,030 --> 00:08:19,031
You people,

104
00:08:19,098 --> 00:08:21,200
how far will you retreat?

105
00:08:21,267 --> 00:08:24,504
In a 5-minute conversation,
3,000 droplets are released,

106
00:08:24,570 --> 00:08:28,274
the same as in a single cough,
and they turn into an aerosol.

107
00:08:28,941 --> 00:08:31,911
Meetings will be held remotely
for the foreseeable future.

108
00:08:31,978 --> 00:08:33,946
Droplet-spreading
"Yes, sirs" are prohibited!

109
00:08:35,381 --> 00:08:37,316
They prohibited "Yes, sirs."

110
00:08:37,383 --> 00:08:38,251
Who cares about that?

111
00:08:38,818 --> 00:08:40,353
Hachisuka.

112
00:08:41,787 --> 00:08:46,692
You've sure come a long way
since you were my gopher.

113
00:08:46,759 --> 00:08:48,728
You're called Acting Hospital Director,

114
00:08:48,794 --> 00:08:50,863
but you're just
Internal Medicine Director.

115
00:08:51,597 --> 00:08:55,334
You're on the same level
as Director of Surgery Ebina here.

116
00:08:55,401 --> 00:08:57,537
That's way lower.

117
00:08:58,104 --> 00:08:59,705
You've got COVID to thank.

118
00:08:59,772 --> 00:09:00,773
Branch Director Hiruma,

119
00:09:00,840 --> 00:09:02,308
that is a tactless remark.

120
00:09:02,375 --> 00:09:05,077
What's tactless is your face.

121
00:09:05,144 --> 00:09:08,214
It's so bland and unremarkable.

122
00:09:10,316 --> 00:09:11,684
This is…

123
00:09:12,418 --> 00:09:16,122
the last line of defense
against the spread of the virus.

124
00:09:16,622 --> 00:09:20,393
If by chance there was an outbreak
at our hospital,

125
00:09:21,093 --> 00:09:24,130
it would bring about a collapse
of Japan's medical system.

126
00:09:24,697 --> 00:09:28,367
Responsibility for that
lies entirely with me!

127
00:09:31,504 --> 00:09:33,606
What kind of bow is that?

128
00:09:33,673 --> 00:09:35,608
The "Yes, sir" pose prevents droplets.

129
00:09:36,108 --> 00:09:37,743
Dr. Hachisuka came up with it.

130
00:09:37,810 --> 00:09:39,078
Is that right?

131
00:09:39,145 --> 00:09:40,846
How overdramatic.

132
00:09:40,913 --> 00:09:43,115
Instead of always calling us together,

133
00:09:43,182 --> 00:09:44,183
from now on,

134
00:09:44,250 --> 00:09:46,652
hold meetings remotely.

135
00:09:48,888 --> 00:09:49,889
Oh, right.

136
00:09:49,956 --> 00:09:51,290
Branch Director Hiruma.

137
00:09:54,026 --> 00:09:57,396
I am concerned about your health, sir.

138
00:09:57,463 --> 00:09:58,864
So from now on,

139
00:09:58,931 --> 00:10:03,302
please perform your duties
remotely from home.

140
00:10:03,369 --> 00:10:06,372
Farewell,

141
00:10:06,939 --> 00:10:08,941
Branch Director Hiruma.

142
00:10:22,321 --> 00:10:23,756
What's wrong?

143
00:10:25,291 --> 00:10:26,192
That riles me!

144
00:10:26,993 --> 00:10:28,628
That really riles me!

145
00:10:28,694 --> 00:10:31,764
<i>The university hospital's once</i>
<i>illustrious Surgery Department</i>

146
00:10:31,831 --> 00:10:33,432
<i>was moved to the branch hospital.</i>

147
00:10:33,499 --> 00:10:36,569
<i>The number of surgeries</i>
<i>was greatly decreased…</i>

148
00:10:36,636 --> 00:10:39,071
<i>and it was running in the red.</i>

149
00:10:43,776 --> 00:10:48,614
There's a great view
of the Director's Office from here.

150
00:10:48,681 --> 00:10:50,683
- Branch Director Hiruma. Excuse me.
- Come in.

151
00:10:50,750 --> 00:10:52,218
Allow me to disinfect your hands.

152
00:10:52,284 --> 00:10:54,053
Thank you.

153
00:10:56,155 --> 00:10:57,089
Thanks.

154
00:10:57,156 --> 00:10:58,791
- Goodbye.
- Bye.

155
00:11:00,059 --> 00:11:01,527
- Branch Director Hiruma.
- Yes?

156
00:11:01,594 --> 00:11:05,631
Once the coronavirus trouble calms down,
we'll be back in charge.

157
00:11:05,698 --> 00:11:06,966
That's right!

158
00:11:07,033 --> 00:11:10,136
We'll return to the main hospital
and make them weep, Branch Director!

159
00:11:10,202 --> 00:11:11,337
- Kaji!
- Yes?

160
00:11:11,904 --> 00:11:13,973
Enough of that "weep branch director"!

161
00:11:15,474 --> 00:11:17,243
- Don't say it.
- I didn't say it.

162
00:11:17,309 --> 00:11:18,177
- Yes, he did.
- Right.

163
00:11:18,244 --> 00:11:19,478
- What?
- You did.

164
00:11:19,545 --> 00:11:20,413
No, I didn't.

165
00:11:21,814 --> 00:11:22,948
<i>Meanwhile,</i>

166
00:11:23,015 --> 00:11:25,885
<i>this freelance maverick doctor…</i>

167
00:11:25,951 --> 00:11:30,222
<i>who was never attached</i>
<i>to any hospital returned.</i>

168
00:11:31,390 --> 00:11:33,492
<i>This woman…</i>

169
00:11:33,559 --> 00:11:34,727
I'm back!

170
00:11:34,794 --> 00:11:36,429
<i>She hates groups,</i>

171
00:11:36,495 --> 00:11:38,097
<i>she hates authorities,</i>

172
00:11:38,164 --> 00:11:39,498
<i>and she hates constraints.</i>

173
00:11:39,565 --> 00:11:42,301
Oh, Ben Casey!

174
00:11:43,002 --> 00:11:46,372
<i>Her weapons are her specialty license</i>
<i>and her skill</i>

175
00:11:46,439 --> 00:11:47,840
<i> to work her way up.</i>

176
00:11:48,674 --> 00:11:51,210
- Surprise!
- Surprise!

177
00:11:51,277 --> 00:11:52,111
What a surprise!

178
00:11:52,178 --> 00:11:54,346
- Welcome back!
- Welcome back!

179
00:11:54,413 --> 00:11:55,748
I'm back!

180
00:11:55,815 --> 00:11:57,883
What? There's more of you.

181
00:11:57,950 --> 00:12:01,554
- This is Ben Casey's son, Gannon.
- Gannon.

182
00:12:02,788 --> 00:12:04,757
Ben Casey's baby?

183
00:12:04,824 --> 00:12:05,791
- That's right!
- Right!

184
00:12:05,858 --> 00:12:08,260
- Really?
- Yes!

185
00:12:08,327 --> 00:12:10,930
- Look at you.
- How cute.

186
00:12:10,996 --> 00:12:16,368
Michiko, thank goodness
you made it back here alive.

187
00:12:16,435 --> 00:12:17,403
Of course, I'm alive.

188
00:12:18,337 --> 00:12:20,339
Since we couldn't contact you,

189
00:12:20,406 --> 00:12:22,742
we thought you had caught
the virus at a New York hospital.

190
00:12:22,808 --> 00:12:25,111
Akira was so worried, he nearly died.

191
00:12:25,177 --> 00:12:27,146
Sorry. I lost my cellphone.

192
00:12:27,213 --> 00:12:28,180
Oh, you!

193
00:12:28,247 --> 00:12:30,816
Welcome back
from your two-week quarantine.

194
00:12:30,883 --> 00:12:32,685
- I was so bored, I thought I would die.
- Here.

195
00:12:32,752 --> 00:12:34,153
Woah!

196
00:12:35,654 --> 00:12:38,224
Due to COVID, patients can't get surgery,

197
00:12:38,290 --> 00:12:39,625
so they're queued up and waiting.

198
00:12:39,692 --> 00:12:42,161
- All right!
- Come on.

199
00:12:42,228 --> 00:12:43,829
First, let's have a drink!

200
00:12:43,896 --> 00:12:47,800
- Okay. Cheers!
- Cheers!

201
00:12:48,400 --> 00:12:50,936
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon.</i>

202
00:12:51,003 --> 00:12:54,073
<i>Also known as… Doctor X.</i>

203
00:12:55,407 --> 00:12:57,710
That's so refreshing!

204
00:13:08,320 --> 00:13:10,556
Michiko! There's meat over here!

205
00:13:10,623 --> 00:13:12,458
Meat? Let me at it!

206
00:13:13,893 --> 00:13:14,727
I'll take some!

207
00:13:28,073 --> 00:13:30,476
Oh, wow!

208
00:13:32,011 --> 00:13:34,346
- You know, this is one splashy party.
- Right.

209
00:13:34,413 --> 00:13:35,748
But this meat looks great.

210
00:13:35,815 --> 00:13:38,517
The party's sponsor
asked you to be here, Michiko.

211
00:13:38,584 --> 00:13:40,920
I hope their prevention measures are okay.

212
00:13:41,453 --> 00:13:43,088
Akira, where's my fork?

213
00:13:43,155 --> 00:13:44,490
- Fork?
- How can I eat this?

214
00:13:44,557 --> 00:13:45,724
Don't worry.

215
00:13:46,458 --> 00:13:48,894
The guests have all tested
negative for COVID

216
00:13:48,961 --> 00:13:51,197
and the party is being held in a bubble.

217
00:13:51,263 --> 00:13:53,666
Well, Representative Hitotsubashi.

218
00:13:53,732 --> 00:13:57,102
Thank you for inviting us
to this lovely party.

219
00:13:57,169 --> 00:13:59,605
This is Michiko Daimon. I represent her.

220
00:14:00,206 --> 00:14:01,440
This woman?

221
00:14:02,441 --> 00:14:04,877
You're dressed awful flashy for a surgeon.

222
00:14:06,579 --> 00:14:09,815
Well, thanks. You're dressed
pretty damn flashy, too.

223
00:14:09,882 --> 00:14:11,650
Don't talk like that.

224
00:14:11,717 --> 00:14:13,719
Sorry for her rude way of speaking.

225
00:14:13,786 --> 00:14:16,722
However, I vouch
for her surgical abilities.

226
00:14:17,289 --> 00:14:18,624
Is she really all right?

227
00:14:18,691 --> 00:14:19,658
I vouch for her, too.

228
00:14:19,725 --> 00:14:22,261
I was at her surgery
on New Zealand's deputy prime minister.

229
00:14:22,328 --> 00:14:23,996
It was exquisite and perfect.

230
00:14:24,063 --> 00:14:25,130
Oh, it's the lamb!

231
00:14:25,998 --> 00:14:27,466
I am Dr. Ichiki. It has been a while.

232
00:14:28,234 --> 00:14:30,736
If my attending physician
Dr. Ichiki says so,

233
00:14:31,370 --> 00:14:33,105
then I'm okay with this flashy doctor.

234
00:14:33,172 --> 00:14:34,006
However,

235
00:14:34,073 --> 00:14:36,575
I've heard the surgical fees
are incredibly exorbitant.

236
00:14:37,910 --> 00:14:39,745
A politician's body is their asset.

237
00:14:39,812 --> 00:14:42,481
I'll pay whatever it takes
as long as she's talented.

238
00:14:42,548 --> 00:14:44,383
- Show her my chart.
- Yes, ma'am.

239
00:14:49,755 --> 00:14:50,789
Well…

240
00:14:51,290 --> 00:14:52,992
It's just gallstone.

241
00:14:53,058 --> 00:14:56,428
We will gladly accept
whatever the surgery is.

242
00:14:56,495 --> 00:14:59,031
In addition to removing the gallstone,

243
00:15:00,432 --> 00:15:02,067
I would like a nip and tuck.

244
00:15:05,237 --> 00:15:07,373
That will cost you extra.

245
00:15:08,007 --> 00:15:09,275
We'll gladly do it.

246
00:15:10,309 --> 00:15:13,379
A politician's face is also their asset.

247
00:15:14,647 --> 00:15:15,981
We need to fix it soon.

248
00:15:16,548 --> 00:15:17,816
Yes, you're right.

249
00:15:17,883 --> 00:15:19,485
You need to fix it soon.

250
00:15:23,956 --> 00:15:26,158
NO ENTRANCE, GREEN ZONE

251
00:15:28,427 --> 00:15:30,863
COVID TESTING

252
00:15:31,430 --> 00:15:32,398
RED ZONE

253
00:15:36,302 --> 00:15:38,003
- Monitor okay.
- I've got the ECMO.

254
00:15:38,070 --> 00:15:40,606
Let's move him. One, two, three!

255
00:15:42,508 --> 00:15:45,711
Number 21's PF ratio has fallen to 110.

256
00:15:45,778 --> 00:15:49,348
We've got the ECMO ready for them,
but the ICU is full.

257
00:15:49,415 --> 00:15:52,384
There are still three beds
in the Circulatory Department.

258
00:15:52,451 --> 00:15:56,355
Switch all ICU beds in the hospital
to use for COVID.

259
00:15:59,959 --> 00:16:01,226
Director Hachisuka,

260
00:16:01,293 --> 00:16:02,895
the live interview is about to start.

261
00:16:12,371 --> 00:16:14,039
Thank you for waiting.

262
00:16:14,773 --> 00:16:17,109
- Please, go ahead.
- Thank you.

263
00:16:18,177 --> 00:16:24,350
<i>As for the advent of this new,</i>
<i>extremely virulent variant,</i>

264
00:16:24,850 --> 00:16:28,587
<i>politicians, government,</i>
<i>and the medical system</i>

265
00:16:28,654 --> 00:16:32,157
<i>should combine forces</i>
<i>in facing this crisis.</i>

266
00:16:32,658 --> 00:16:34,259
<i>Already,</i>

267
00:16:34,326 --> 00:16:37,896
<i>all our hospital's ICU units</i>
<i>are used for COVID.</i>

268
00:16:38,430 --> 00:16:41,166
<i>We are thoroughly prepared</i>
<i>for accepting patients.</i>

269
00:16:41,233 --> 00:16:42,234
Here we go.

270
00:16:44,269 --> 00:16:45,237
Here goes!

271
00:16:49,208 --> 00:16:50,075
You can do it.

272
00:16:50,743 --> 00:16:52,077
Thank you for this meal.

273
00:16:52,144 --> 00:16:53,345
MASAKO OHMA, NURSE

274
00:16:53,412 --> 00:16:55,114
Hey, Nurse Ohma. Aren't you hungry?

275
00:16:55,180 --> 00:16:58,650
The stress here is outrageous.
It must affect your appetite.

276
00:16:58,717 --> 00:17:00,786
You'll collapse if you don't eat properly.

277
00:17:03,288 --> 00:17:05,190
Oh, is that TikTok?

278
00:17:05,924 --> 00:17:08,360
Watching TikTok cheers you up,
doesn't it, Nurse Ohma?

279
00:17:08,427 --> 00:17:11,230
<i>I'm at a pretty amazing place today.</i>

280
00:17:11,296 --> 00:17:13,632
Oh, it's the cosplayer Akari Akase.

281
00:17:13,699 --> 00:17:15,367
She's cute, isn't she?

282
00:17:15,434 --> 00:17:16,435
But lately,

283
00:17:16,502 --> 00:17:18,937
she doesn't make me laugh anymore.

284
00:17:19,605 --> 00:17:20,706
<i>Today,</i>

285
00:17:21,206 --> 00:17:23,575
<i>I'm at a party for a Diet representative.</i>

286
00:17:24,109 --> 00:17:25,411
<i>I'm not a party person.</i>

287
00:17:26,211 --> 00:17:29,148
<i>Representative Hitotsubashi</i>
<i>went to my high school.</i>

288
00:17:29,214 --> 00:17:30,616
<i>I support her.</i>

289
00:17:30,682 --> 00:17:32,151
Yes, that's not much fun.

290
00:17:32,217 --> 00:17:34,386
I'm going to stop following her channel.

291
00:17:34,453 --> 00:17:35,687
I'll stop liking her, too.

292
00:17:35,754 --> 00:17:37,823
You know, no matter how hard we try,

293
00:17:37,890 --> 00:17:40,359
people like her keep the pandemic
from ending!

294
00:17:40,426 --> 00:17:41,427
That's for sure.

295
00:17:43,495 --> 00:17:44,763
Dr. Daimon!

296
00:17:45,497 --> 00:17:46,532
What?

297
00:17:46,598 --> 00:17:47,666
It's Dr. Daimon!

298
00:17:49,401 --> 00:17:51,670
<i>Someone really seems</i>
<i>to be enjoying the meat.</i>

299
00:17:52,304 --> 00:17:54,406
- Dr. Daimon?
- Demon?

300
00:17:54,473 --> 00:17:56,275
- "Demon?"
- Who's that?

301
00:17:56,341 --> 00:17:58,043
She's shoveling down the meat.

302
00:17:58,110 --> 00:17:59,711
She's a demon-like doctor.

303
00:17:59,778 --> 00:18:01,947
If she catches COVID, I won't help her!

304
00:18:02,014 --> 00:18:04,283
She deserves it.
Don't blame me if you get sick.

305
00:18:07,786 --> 00:18:09,521
Michiko, I'll get you seconds.

306
00:18:09,588 --> 00:18:11,256
Really? I'll go, too.

307
00:18:16,261 --> 00:18:17,096
Hey,

308
00:18:17,162 --> 00:18:18,464
aren't you going to eat?

309
00:18:19,498 --> 00:18:21,400
When I was in Africa,
there weren't even masks

310
00:18:21,467 --> 00:18:24,536
or water to wash your hands,
let alone meat like this.

311
00:18:25,337 --> 00:18:26,939
There weren't any vaccines either.

312
00:18:27,506 --> 00:18:28,340
Africa?

313
00:18:28,407 --> 00:18:30,209
Doctors Across Borders.

314
00:18:30,275 --> 00:18:31,677
After New Zealand,

315
00:18:31,743 --> 00:18:34,079
I visited impoverished countries
in Africa.

316
00:18:35,180 --> 00:18:36,748
Then why are you at this party?

317
00:18:38,584 --> 00:18:41,653
I became a doctor, thanks to a scholarship
from this foundation.

318
00:18:43,489 --> 00:18:44,656
I owe them.

319
00:18:48,961 --> 00:18:49,895
Dr. Daimon,

320
00:18:49,962 --> 00:18:52,164
how long were you
at that hospital in New York?

321
00:18:53,398 --> 00:18:55,067
About a year and a half.

322
00:18:55,134 --> 00:18:57,769
That was when the pandemic
was at its height.

323
00:18:57,836 --> 00:18:59,605
Why did you go then?

324
00:18:59,671 --> 00:19:01,740
There was a patient
waiting for surgery there.

325
00:19:02,574 --> 00:19:04,076
"Because it's there," huh?

326
00:19:05,477 --> 00:19:07,312
Spoken like a true mountain climber.

327
00:19:07,379 --> 00:19:08,213
What?

328
00:19:09,381 --> 00:19:11,216
Any doctor would do the same.

329
00:19:26,198 --> 00:19:27,099
Are you all right?

330
00:19:27,166 --> 00:19:28,534
Let me feel that part.

331
00:19:30,202 --> 00:19:31,737
Cholecystitis.

332
00:19:33,605 --> 00:19:35,674
There's a tumor on the gallbladder.

333
00:19:35,741 --> 00:19:37,709
It will be too late unless we operate now!

334
00:19:37,776 --> 00:19:39,311
Isn't it just a gallstone?

335
00:19:39,378 --> 00:19:40,279
Oh, dear!

336
00:19:40,345 --> 00:19:41,513
Call an ambulance!

337
00:19:49,521 --> 00:19:50,389
Stand back!

338
00:19:54,760 --> 00:19:55,661
Hurry!

339
00:19:57,029 --> 00:19:59,298
You rode in the ambulance dressed in that?

340
00:19:59,364 --> 00:20:02,334
Wherever you go, Dr. Daimon,
patients always appear.

341
00:20:02,401 --> 00:20:03,669
Shut up! Hurry!

342
00:20:07,739 --> 00:20:08,607
Wait!

343
00:20:08,674 --> 00:20:10,576
You need to take a COVID test first.

344
00:20:11,577 --> 00:20:13,078
Dr. Daimon!

345
00:20:14,079 --> 00:20:15,080
I'm Nurse Ohma.

346
00:20:15,147 --> 00:20:16,481
Do the test in the tent outside.

347
00:20:16,548 --> 00:20:17,583
Let's go.

348
00:20:18,183 --> 00:20:19,184
Fools!

349
00:20:20,419 --> 00:20:23,088
This person is no ordinary patient.

350
00:20:25,791 --> 00:20:27,192
Representative Hitotsubashi,

351
00:20:27,259 --> 00:20:29,394
we'll get you tested in a private room.

352
00:20:30,229 --> 00:20:31,263
It hurts…

353
00:20:32,097 --> 00:20:34,833
Acute cholecystitis
and possible gallbladder cancer.

354
00:20:34,900 --> 00:20:36,068
I'll operate immediately.

355
00:20:40,105 --> 00:20:42,307
I want this doctor to operate.

356
00:20:47,546 --> 00:20:49,581
Leave this to me. Dr. Hachisuka.

357
00:20:49,648 --> 00:20:51,516
I'll get an OR ready right away.

358
00:20:52,451 --> 00:20:53,552
Yes, sir. Right away.

359
00:21:00,392 --> 00:21:01,526
Hold it right there.

360
00:21:05,163 --> 00:21:10,035
Representative Hitotsubashi
is a rare politician who understands

361
00:21:10,102 --> 00:21:11,937
the future role of medicine in Japan.

362
00:21:12,738 --> 00:21:13,772
In the near future,

363
00:21:13,839 --> 00:21:16,908
she may even become
Japan's first female prime minister.

364
00:21:18,076 --> 00:21:19,111
So?

365
00:21:21,546 --> 00:21:26,118
Can you swear that you will perform
a 100% perfect surgery?

366
00:21:27,953 --> 00:21:30,122
Not 98 or 99%.

367
00:21:30,188 --> 00:21:33,058
It must be 100% perfect.

368
00:21:34,059 --> 00:21:35,761
There are no doctors like that.

369
00:21:35,827 --> 00:21:37,229
Doctors are only human.

370
00:21:46,538 --> 00:21:47,539
I…

371
00:21:48,540 --> 00:21:50,175
will not fail.

372
00:22:00,852 --> 00:22:04,823
We will perform an extended right
hepatectomy on Yuka Hitotsubashi.

373
00:22:04,890 --> 00:22:06,258
Let's begin.

374
00:22:06,325 --> 00:22:07,259
- Yes, sir.
- Yes, sir.

375
00:22:07,326 --> 00:22:10,095
BP 122 over 75, normal sinus rhythm.

376
00:22:10,162 --> 00:22:11,530
- Scalpel.
- Here.

377
00:22:17,102 --> 00:22:18,103
- Bovie.
- Here.

378
00:22:25,077 --> 00:22:27,312
- Inject the steroids.
- Got it.

379
00:22:41,360 --> 00:22:42,861
She's fast.

380
00:22:43,362 --> 00:22:45,063
<i>Michiko Daimon?</i>

381
00:22:46,231 --> 00:22:48,166
<i>She's operating here?</i>

382
00:22:48,233 --> 00:22:52,070
Yes. The patient is Diet representative
Yuka Hitotsubashi.

383
00:22:52,137 --> 00:22:53,972
<i>Why is Daimon operating?</i>

384
00:22:54,039 --> 00:22:56,641
Apparently, Dr. Hachisuka approved it.

385
00:22:57,542 --> 00:22:58,810
Damn it all!

386
00:22:59,411 --> 00:23:03,115
Is he taking over Surgery, too,
while I'm away?

387
00:23:03,181 --> 00:23:05,884
Dear, be careful.
You're spreading droplets.

388
00:23:05,951 --> 00:23:07,386
Oh, I'm sorry.

389
00:23:07,452 --> 00:23:11,757
I just thought I would like to shout
a little in my own home.

390
00:23:11,823 --> 00:23:13,358
You sure are upset.

391
00:23:13,425 --> 00:23:14,760
Must be exhaustion from COVID.

392
00:23:15,894 --> 00:23:18,163
Damn that Hachisuka.

393
00:23:18,230 --> 00:23:20,699
Forcing me to work remotely like this.

394
00:23:20,766 --> 00:23:22,367
I can't get used to it!

395
00:23:22,968 --> 00:23:24,903
Tell that Hachisuka he's a jerk!

396
00:23:24,970 --> 00:23:26,371
Yes, sir!

397
00:23:26,438 --> 00:23:27,906
<i>You jerk!</i>

398
00:23:28,440 --> 00:23:30,108
What? Branch Director Hiruma?

399
00:23:30,175 --> 00:23:31,076
<i>What?</i>

400
00:23:31,643 --> 00:23:33,412
- Branch Director Hiruma?
<i>- What?</i>

401
00:23:33,478 --> 00:23:34,312
What?

402
00:23:34,379 --> 00:23:36,581
You're frozen.

403
00:23:36,648 --> 00:23:38,417
Frozen? What is?

404
00:23:38,950 --> 00:23:41,586
I'm not a hunk of tofu!

405
00:23:41,653 --> 00:23:42,587
What a weird face.

406
00:23:42,654 --> 00:23:43,955
It sure is.

407
00:23:44,022 --> 00:23:45,991
- Oh, fix it!
- Hold on.

408
00:23:46,057 --> 00:23:47,259
Get rid of it!

409
00:23:50,462 --> 00:23:52,597
Right upper lobe removal complete.

410
00:23:52,664 --> 00:23:54,266
Next, ablate the intrahepatic duct.

411
00:23:54,332 --> 00:23:55,667
- Metz.
- Here.

412
00:24:11,249 --> 00:24:15,053
She is really quite fast,
but will it be all right?

413
00:24:15,754 --> 00:24:17,756
"I will not fail," she says.

414
00:24:17,823 --> 00:24:20,058
Sounds like overconfidence to me.

415
00:24:21,059 --> 00:24:21,960
No.

416
00:24:22,861 --> 00:24:26,064
This isn't just 99%.

417
00:24:26,131 --> 00:24:28,567
It is truly 100% perfect!

418
00:24:41,446 --> 00:24:44,049
This feels great!

419
00:24:44,115 --> 00:24:48,019
Japanese bathhouses are the best!

420
00:24:51,990 --> 00:24:53,758
<i>Congratulations, Michiko.</i>

421
00:24:53,825 --> 00:24:56,695
You've won the favor of Director
of Internal Medicine Hachisuka.

422
00:24:57,262 --> 00:24:58,096
His favor?

423
00:24:58,163 --> 00:25:01,399
He wants you
in the Totei University Hospital.

424
00:25:01,466 --> 00:25:04,769
We have <i>taiyaki</i> to celebrate your job.

425
00:25:06,171 --> 00:25:08,340
- No wonder there are so many.
- That's right.

426
00:25:08,406 --> 00:25:11,243
All right! I'll dig right in!

427
00:25:12,644 --> 00:25:13,745
- Delicious.
- Yes.

428
00:25:13,812 --> 00:25:15,480
It has been so long!

429
00:25:16,381 --> 00:25:18,717
Who is that female doctor?

430
00:25:19,985 --> 00:25:21,987
Get me the documents on her.

431
00:25:22,053 --> 00:25:25,757
Her work history, surgery stats,
surgery papers, everything.

432
00:25:28,593 --> 00:25:33,298
<i>When Ryutaro Hachisuka was young,</i>
<i>he was a surgeon.</i>

433
00:25:33,365 --> 00:25:35,534
<i>But he was an insufferable perfectionist.</i>

434
00:25:35,600 --> 00:25:39,037
<i>The university hospital</i>
<i>professors tormented him.</i>

435
00:25:39,104 --> 00:25:41,740
<i>That's when he started working</i>

436
00:25:41,806 --> 00:25:44,543
<i>at the National Institute</i>
<i>of Infectious Disease Research.</i>

437
00:25:44,609 --> 00:25:49,080
Then, thanks to the pandemic,
he started moving up in the world.

438
00:25:49,147 --> 00:25:51,917
While the hospital director
works remotely from the US,

439
00:25:51,983 --> 00:25:54,986
he's in control of the hospital
as the acting hospital director.

440
00:25:55,687 --> 00:25:58,023
So some people benefit from COVID, huh?

441
00:25:58,089 --> 00:25:59,157
That's right.

442
00:25:59,224 --> 00:26:02,193
And that old Hiruma
somehow made a comeback, too.

443
00:26:02,260 --> 00:26:03,962
The old professors

444
00:26:04,029 --> 00:26:05,297
are afraid of catching COVID,

445
00:26:05,363 --> 00:26:06,865
so they all stay at home.

446
00:26:06,932 --> 00:26:09,601
Nobody else wanted to become
the branch hospital director.

447
00:26:09,668 --> 00:26:11,503
So that's how it happened.

448
00:26:11,570 --> 00:26:14,940
That guy just adores the hospital.

449
00:26:15,006 --> 00:26:16,541
Meeting room forever!

450
00:26:16,608 --> 00:26:18,376
Doctors' processions forever!

451
00:26:18,443 --> 00:26:20,879
- What? That's really crazy.
- I know.

452
00:26:20,946 --> 00:26:23,114
- Oh, dear.
- Michiko, I'm glad you're back.

453
00:26:23,181 --> 00:26:24,849
Yes. I'm really glad, too!

454
00:26:24,916 --> 00:26:28,753
I'm glad that you came back, too, Michiko.

455
00:26:28,820 --> 00:26:30,789
<i>- Ron!</i>
- Oh, no!

456
00:26:30,855 --> 00:26:35,594
<i>Richi, chitoi dora-dora,</i>
and <i>dora-dora haneman.</i>

457
00:26:35,660 --> 00:26:38,563
<i>Dora-dora-dora-dora!</i> Congratulations!

458
00:26:38,630 --> 00:26:40,832
- I don't mind at all!
- You don't seem like yourself…

459
00:26:40,899 --> 00:26:43,268
SURGERY BRANCH

460
00:26:43,335 --> 00:26:44,903
<i>All of you,</i>

461
00:26:45,403 --> 00:26:50,475
as surgeons of our great
Totei University Hospital,

462
00:26:50,542 --> 00:26:54,412
I want you to have pride
as you participate in…

463
00:26:55,313 --> 00:26:57,649
this traditional director's rounds.

464
00:26:57,716 --> 00:26:58,917
- Yes, sir!
- Yes, sir!

465
00:26:58,984 --> 00:27:01,353
It's great that we can do
this doctors' procession!

466
00:27:01,419 --> 00:27:02,721
Don't group up though.

467
00:27:02,787 --> 00:27:04,823
Maintain plenty of distance.

468
00:27:04,889 --> 00:27:06,391
- Yes, sir!
- Yes, sir!

469
00:27:06,458 --> 00:27:07,926
- Shall we go?
- Yes, sir!

470
00:27:09,861 --> 00:27:10,795
<i>At this time,</i>

471
00:27:11,663 --> 00:27:15,600
<i>Branch Director Hiruma will conduct</i>
<i>the branch director's rounds.</i>

472
00:27:26,745 --> 00:27:27,879
Demon.

473
00:27:27,946 --> 00:27:29,314
Hey! Dr. Daimon!

474
00:27:31,182 --> 00:27:32,484
Not her again.

475
00:27:32,550 --> 00:27:35,153
She was pigging out on meat
on that livestream.

476
00:27:37,322 --> 00:27:38,823
Well…

477
00:27:38,890 --> 00:27:41,493
it has been a while, Dr. Michiko Daimon.

478
00:27:41,559 --> 00:27:43,561
- Hello.
- Hello.

479
00:27:44,062 --> 00:27:47,666
For a freelance
part-time doctor as yourself,

480
00:27:47,732 --> 00:27:52,337
it must be hard to get work
during this COVID crisis.

481
00:27:52,404 --> 00:27:54,305
Are you looking for work today?

482
00:27:55,740 --> 00:27:58,143
It has been a long time,
Branch Director Hiruma.

483
00:27:58,209 --> 00:27:59,177
Hello.

484
00:27:59,244 --> 00:28:02,180
Our Michiko Daimon
will be working with you again.

485
00:28:02,247 --> 00:28:03,248
What?

486
00:28:03,314 --> 00:28:04,549
There must be some mistake.

487
00:28:05,116 --> 00:28:05,950
Right now,

488
00:28:06,017 --> 00:28:08,086
our Totei University Hospital

489
00:28:08,153 --> 00:28:10,855
cannot hire a part-time doctor.

490
00:28:11,623 --> 00:28:15,593
You're still doing this totally pointless
doctors' procession?

491
00:28:15,660 --> 00:28:16,861
What did you…

492
00:28:16,928 --> 00:28:17,862
- Hey!
- Hey!

493
00:28:17,929 --> 00:28:20,899
Dr. Daimon says it's totally pointless.

494
00:28:20,965 --> 00:28:22,434
Wait!

495
00:28:26,738 --> 00:28:27,739
<i>Dr. Daimon,</i>

496
00:28:28,239 --> 00:28:30,975
your emergency surgery
the other day was magnificent.

497
00:28:31,976 --> 00:28:33,178
It was magnificent.

498
00:28:34,979 --> 00:28:38,249
Yuka Hitotsubashi's recovery
from surgery is going smoothly.

499
00:28:38,983 --> 00:28:40,251
Dr. Ichiki,

500
00:28:40,318 --> 00:28:42,687
you are a respiratory surgery
specialist, right?

501
00:28:42,754 --> 00:28:44,055
Yes.

502
00:28:44,122 --> 00:28:47,692
Since the spread of COVID
will continue for a while,

503
00:28:47,759 --> 00:28:50,962
we need people with your special skills.

504
00:28:51,029 --> 00:28:52,397
Nice to have you.

505
00:28:58,369 --> 00:28:59,904
I'm counting on you.

506
00:28:59,971 --> 00:29:01,473
It's nice to have you.

507
00:29:03,908 --> 00:29:06,377
Akira, before anything else…

508
00:29:06,444 --> 00:29:10,682
Allow me to review
Michiko Daimon's contract requirements.

509
00:29:11,883 --> 00:29:13,051
Contract requirements?

510
00:29:18,523 --> 00:29:19,457
Here.

511
00:29:21,593 --> 00:29:22,527
Here.

512
00:29:25,230 --> 00:29:26,331
Here.

513
00:29:26,898 --> 00:29:28,299
If you would, please.

514
00:29:29,968 --> 00:29:30,835
Here.

515
00:29:36,407 --> 00:29:39,577
I've sent this to the surgeons as well.

516
00:29:39,644 --> 00:29:41,312
Please have a look.

517
00:29:46,818 --> 00:29:49,587
"Assisting with professors' papers."

518
00:29:49,654 --> 00:29:50,722
I won't do it.

519
00:29:50,789 --> 00:29:52,123
"Attending conferences."

520
00:29:52,190 --> 00:29:53,124
I won't do it.

521
00:29:53,191 --> 00:29:55,660
- "Driving superiors to golf."
- I won't do it.

522
00:29:55,727 --> 00:29:58,062
- "Going out drinking."
- I won't do it.

523
00:29:58,797 --> 00:30:00,265
"Covering up love affairs."

524
00:30:00,331 --> 00:30:01,733
I won't do it.

525
00:30:03,034 --> 00:30:04,769
I couldn't agree more.

526
00:30:06,237 --> 00:30:10,875
<i>Director of Internal Medicine Hachisuka,</i>
<i>how can you say that?</i>

527
00:30:11,409 --> 00:30:14,145
<i>"Director rounds</i>
<i>and branch director rounds."</i>

528
00:30:14,212 --> 00:30:15,280
I won't do it.

529
00:30:15,346 --> 00:30:18,783
<i>Hey, Dr. Daimon, that's disrespectful</i>
<i>to the branch director.</i>

530
00:30:18,850 --> 00:30:21,786
<i>Take that one back! By the way,</i>
<i>I'm Director of Surgery again.</i>

531
00:30:21,853 --> 00:30:22,987
Keep reading.

532
00:30:23,054 --> 00:30:25,056
<i>- You're ignoring me?</i>
<i>- Damn you!</i>

533
00:30:25,690 --> 00:30:27,826
We're doing this again?

534
00:30:28,426 --> 00:30:30,094
- There's more than before.
- What?

535
00:30:31,262 --> 00:30:34,032
"Remote meeting hosting"? What's that?

536
00:30:34,098 --> 00:30:36,267
<i>- I won't do it.</i>
- What?

537
00:30:36,334 --> 00:30:39,470
"Assisting with remote
computer difficulties."

538
00:30:39,537 --> 00:30:40,839
<i>I won't do it.</i>

539
00:30:40,905 --> 00:30:43,241
"Assisting with connecting
to Wi-Fi for remote meetings."

540
00:30:43,308 --> 00:30:44,609
I won't do it.

541
00:30:44,676 --> 00:30:46,544
"Attending remote drinking parties."

542
00:30:47,579 --> 00:30:48,413
I won't do it.

543
00:30:48,479 --> 00:30:50,181
You won't do anything remote either?

544
00:30:50,248 --> 00:30:53,484
- Hey, who said you could do that?
- Don't you do anything?

545
00:30:53,551 --> 00:30:55,420
And so on and so forth.

546
00:30:55,486 --> 00:30:58,623
Any job that does not require
a medical license…

547
00:30:58,690 --> 00:31:00,425
I won't do any of it.

548
00:31:02,594 --> 00:31:04,529
Understood.

549
00:31:04,596 --> 00:31:06,865
<i>Hey! Dr. Hachisuka!</i>

550
00:31:06,931 --> 00:31:09,400
<i>How dare you approve of this, you jerk!</i>

551
00:31:12,570 --> 00:31:13,771
That is all.

552
00:31:24,649 --> 00:31:26,384
I look forward to working with you.

553
00:31:31,723 --> 00:31:32,924
I won't do it.

554
00:31:33,591 --> 00:31:36,094
I don't need a medical license to do that.

555
00:31:41,866 --> 00:31:43,234
There's an emergency!

556
00:31:43,735 --> 00:31:46,504
Among guests
at Representative Hitotsubashi's party…

557
00:31:47,105 --> 00:31:48,640
there has been a COVID outbreak.

558
00:31:48,706 --> 00:31:49,908
An outbreak?

559
00:31:49,974 --> 00:31:53,011
There have already been
18 confirmed cases.

560
00:31:59,117 --> 00:32:00,551
What?

561
00:32:01,119 --> 00:32:04,455
But everyone took a COVID test

562
00:32:04,522 --> 00:32:06,557
and we had scrupulous
prevention measures in place.

563
00:32:06,624 --> 00:32:08,126
I can't believe it.

564
00:32:13,665 --> 00:32:15,533
Are the COVID test results back?

565
00:32:17,068 --> 00:32:18,770
You're negative.

566
00:32:20,605 --> 00:32:22,840
Then I can check out of this hospital.

567
00:32:22,907 --> 00:32:24,442
I'll call you a car.

568
00:32:24,509 --> 00:32:26,444
You can't check out.

569
00:32:28,379 --> 00:32:29,580
Dr. Daimon.

570
00:32:30,114 --> 00:32:31,382
My surgery went well, right?

571
00:32:31,449 --> 00:32:33,785
Of course. It was 100% perfect.

572
00:32:33,851 --> 00:32:34,919
Then why?

573
00:32:34,986 --> 00:32:37,789
There was an outbreak at your party.

574
00:32:37,855 --> 00:32:39,524
You'll quarantine for a while.

575
00:32:39,590 --> 00:32:40,625
Quarantine?

576
00:32:41,459 --> 00:32:42,727
I am very busy.

577
00:32:42,794 --> 00:32:44,395
There's an election in the fall.

578
00:32:47,432 --> 00:32:49,200
Talking to you is hopeless!

579
00:32:50,134 --> 00:32:51,235
Get me Dr. Hachisuka.

580
00:32:51,302 --> 00:32:52,203
Enough of that.

581
00:32:55,106 --> 00:32:58,443
Your prevention measures were a failure.

582
00:33:08,720 --> 00:33:10,521
Don't go threatening a politician.

583
00:33:14,225 --> 00:33:15,226
Hey.

584
00:33:15,293 --> 00:33:16,661
What's the matter?

585
00:33:18,596 --> 00:33:19,597
It's nothing.

586
00:33:23,634 --> 00:33:27,005
Our operating rooms have been
taken over by Internal Medicine!

587
00:33:28,006 --> 00:33:30,908
They'll be turned into ICU units
with ECMO devices

588
00:33:30,975 --> 00:33:32,877
for the seriously ill.

589
00:33:37,348 --> 00:33:39,751
If this situation continues,

590
00:33:40,284 --> 00:33:42,086
this branch hospital will be…

591
00:33:44,188 --> 00:33:45,390
bankrupt!

592
00:33:46,591 --> 00:33:47,592
Yes.

593
00:33:50,895 --> 00:33:52,563
- Ready the ECMO!
- Yes, sir!

594
00:33:52,630 --> 00:33:53,998
- Hurry!
- Yes, sir.

595
00:33:55,533 --> 00:33:57,368
SURGERY DEPARTMENT

596
00:34:01,939 --> 00:34:03,341
Oh, hey!

597
00:34:03,408 --> 00:34:04,609
Are you all right?

598
00:34:05,209 --> 00:34:06,244
Sorry!

599
00:34:10,048 --> 00:34:14,452
We've all hardly slept
and we haven't been home in months.

600
00:34:14,519 --> 00:34:16,487
All to keep COVID out of our homes.

601
00:34:16,554 --> 00:34:20,058
With increasing tests and patients,
we're short on doctors and nurses.

602
00:34:20,124 --> 00:34:21,192
Hey, Demon!

603
00:34:21,259 --> 00:34:22,994
You were at that party, too, right?

604
00:34:23,061 --> 00:34:25,229
You sure have it good.

605
00:34:27,565 --> 00:34:31,569
We could catch it anytime,
but we're always at the hospital.

606
00:34:32,103 --> 00:34:33,237
We're exhausted!

607
00:34:33,304 --> 00:34:35,139
My wife is a nurse, too,

608
00:34:35,206 --> 00:34:37,575
but day care centers won't take our kids!

609
00:34:37,642 --> 00:34:39,977
We're the ones fighting COVID,

610
00:34:40,044 --> 00:34:42,480
so why do we have to suffer
all these hardships?

611
00:34:42,547 --> 00:34:46,350
It's selfish people like you
who go out and spread COVID.

612
00:34:46,417 --> 00:34:49,821
Think of us who have to deal
with all these COVID patients!

613
00:34:49,887 --> 00:34:52,390
Dr. Daimon only went
because her patient invited her.

614
00:34:52,457 --> 00:34:54,358
We've both been vaccinated
three times overseas.

615
00:34:54,425 --> 00:34:57,528
- Get off your high horse.
- Anyone can catch COVID.

616
00:34:57,595 --> 00:34:59,864
I don't think you should be blaming them.

617
00:34:59,931 --> 00:35:02,834
You don't? Who am I supposed to blame?

618
00:35:02,900 --> 00:35:05,336
- Oh, shut up, would you?
- So you don't have an answer?

619
00:35:08,239 --> 00:35:11,175
Doctors should just shut up
and cure people.

620
00:35:11,242 --> 00:35:13,711
Quit your whining, you idiot.

621
00:35:13,778 --> 00:35:15,413
Whining?

622
00:35:15,480 --> 00:35:17,181
How dare you say that stuff?

623
00:35:17,248 --> 00:35:19,584
Your brain must be full of the virus!

624
00:35:34,465 --> 00:35:38,402
It still hurts where you kicked me,
Dr. Daimon.

625
00:35:39,770 --> 00:35:40,872
Really?

626
00:35:41,706 --> 00:35:43,241
It still hurts?

627
00:35:43,307 --> 00:35:45,243
But nothing was broken.

628
00:35:47,612 --> 00:35:48,813
It must be stress.

629
00:35:52,783 --> 00:35:57,421
I wonder if doctors really work
for other people's sake.

630
00:36:02,026 --> 00:36:05,563
I've lost sight of why I became a doctor.

631
00:36:09,433 --> 00:36:14,272
My family was poor.
So after high school, I did other work.

632
00:36:15,706 --> 00:36:19,844
But I wanted to become a doctor,
so I could save others.

633
00:36:21,512 --> 00:36:24,215
So I got a scholarship
and went to medical school.

634
00:36:25,149 --> 00:36:26,184
Really?

635
00:36:27,418 --> 00:36:29,654
I struggled a lot
to finally become a doctor.

636
00:36:30,588 --> 00:36:34,158
But now, while I train others
how to use an ECMO…

637
00:36:37,295 --> 00:36:40,097
I'm frightened
that I might catch COVID, too.

638
00:36:42,733 --> 00:36:44,735
How much longer will this continue?

639
00:36:45,636 --> 00:36:47,805
I feel like I'll snap from the stress.

640
00:36:51,375 --> 00:36:52,376
Sorry.

641
00:36:52,443 --> 00:36:53,811
This is whining, too, isn't it?

642
00:36:56,747 --> 00:36:57,748
Now,

643
00:36:57,815 --> 00:36:59,817
you little lost lamb.

644
00:37:01,819 --> 00:37:03,454
Were you lost in Africa, too?

645
00:37:06,157 --> 00:37:07,091
No.

646
00:37:08,159 --> 00:37:09,760
There was no time for that.

647
00:37:11,062 --> 00:37:14,332
Other diseases besides COVID
were still spreading in Africa.

648
00:37:18,002 --> 00:37:19,437
Those dying from them…

649
00:37:21,539 --> 00:37:23,841
All I could do was watch them die.

650
00:37:29,413 --> 00:37:31,415
It must have been awful
in New York as well.

651
00:37:37,388 --> 00:37:38,623
It was a war zone.

652
00:38:06,117 --> 00:38:09,720
Every day, I saw many patients
and other doctors pass away.

653
00:38:11,489 --> 00:38:14,058
I've never seen so many patients die.

654
00:38:19,330 --> 00:38:20,631
Doctors, you see,

655
00:38:22,333 --> 00:38:24,568
they don't do it for other people.

656
00:38:24,635 --> 00:38:26,937
It's presumptuous to think that way.

657
00:38:28,105 --> 00:38:29,173
Presumptuous?

658
00:38:29,240 --> 00:38:30,775
That's right.

659
00:38:30,841 --> 00:38:34,378
The patient's virus could kill them
before they ever save them.

660
00:38:35,346 --> 00:38:38,582
They're just another weak
biological creature.

661
00:38:43,554 --> 00:38:44,689
Even so,

662
00:38:46,490 --> 00:38:48,826
it's a doctor's duty
to save their patients, right?

663
00:38:51,629 --> 00:38:53,397
Am I…

664
00:38:55,966 --> 00:38:57,702
prepared to go that far?

665
00:38:58,903 --> 00:39:00,171
Or am I not?

666
00:39:12,416 --> 00:39:13,417
Thank you.

667
00:39:26,964 --> 00:39:30,000
The operating rooms
were taken over by Internal Medicine?

668
00:39:30,768 --> 00:39:33,637
Now, people who could be saved
by Surgery can't be saved.

669
00:39:33,704 --> 00:39:35,039
It's the end of the world!

670
00:39:35,106 --> 00:39:36,774
My business is done for.

671
00:39:36,841 --> 00:39:37,942
Ouch!

672
00:39:38,008 --> 00:39:40,044
That hurts!

673
00:39:40,111 --> 00:39:41,312
Be careful.

674
00:39:42,346 --> 00:39:45,683
Aren't you worried about me?
You're so cold.

675
00:39:45,750 --> 00:39:47,918
Look. Subcutaneous bleeding.

676
00:40:17,581 --> 00:40:18,416
Quit?

677
00:40:18,482 --> 00:40:20,751
Hold on! You just got here!

678
00:40:20,818 --> 00:40:22,353
Abuse from Dr. Daimon, right?

679
00:40:22,420 --> 00:40:24,889
I made up my mind
after consulting with Dr. Daimon.

680
00:40:24,955 --> 00:40:26,223
Oh, man.

681
00:40:26,290 --> 00:40:28,092
That's the worst person to consult with.

682
00:40:28,159 --> 00:40:30,261
Would you look at this barren atmosphere?

683
00:40:30,327 --> 00:40:32,062
We're really short on doctors!

684
00:40:32,129 --> 00:40:34,064
Did you get a better offer from somewhere?

685
00:40:34,131 --> 00:40:34,965
No.

686
00:40:35,032 --> 00:40:37,935
I'm going back to Africa
to start over again.

687
00:40:40,838 --> 00:40:42,573
LETTER OF RESIGNATION

688
00:40:42,640 --> 00:40:43,507
Dr. Daimon!

689
00:40:43,574 --> 00:40:46,110
I won't stop you from quitting,
but you need to get tests.

690
00:40:46,177 --> 00:40:49,046
I did a COVID test this morning.

691
00:40:49,113 --> 00:40:50,848
You've got a slight fever.

692
00:40:50,915 --> 00:40:52,550
- Come with me.
- What?

693
00:40:52,616 --> 00:40:55,019
Disinfect that letter of resignation!

694
00:40:58,255 --> 00:40:59,523
When did your fever start?

695
00:40:59,590 --> 00:41:00,958
It's just a slight cold.

696
00:41:01,025 --> 00:41:02,893
I'm so exhausted. It won't get better.

697
00:41:02,960 --> 00:41:04,495
Where in Africa were you?

698
00:41:04,562 --> 00:41:07,097
Nigeria? Guinea? Sierra Leone? Liberia?

699
00:41:07,164 --> 00:41:08,966
I went to all of them. What about it?

700
00:41:09,033 --> 00:41:10,701
I am perfectly fine!

701
00:41:14,905 --> 00:41:15,873
See!

702
00:41:16,373 --> 00:41:17,575
Are you okay?

703
00:41:23,647 --> 00:41:26,150
- Dr. Ichiki!
- Hey!

704
00:41:26,650 --> 00:41:28,486
- Are you okay?
- Don't touch him!

705
00:41:31,889 --> 00:41:35,025
Possible acute pericarditis. Prep an OR.

706
00:41:35,092 --> 00:41:36,393
- Hurry!
- Yes, ma'am!

707
00:41:36,894 --> 00:41:37,795
I'll help!

708
00:41:37,862 --> 00:41:39,597
Don't touch him! Get back!

709
00:41:39,663 --> 00:41:40,931
Okay.

710
00:42:01,519 --> 00:42:03,087
Dr. Daimon…

711
00:42:05,623 --> 00:42:06,690
Am I…

712
00:42:08,759 --> 00:42:10,060
I swear I'll save you.

713
00:42:11,128 --> 00:42:12,129
Sleep for a while.

714
00:42:20,571 --> 00:42:23,007
What is she doing this time?

715
00:42:23,073 --> 00:42:24,608
She says she'll do it alone.

716
00:42:24,675 --> 00:42:26,911
There's no way she can do it alone.

717
00:42:27,478 --> 00:42:29,146
Surgeries are prohibited!

718
00:42:29,213 --> 00:42:30,681
What's this all about?

719
00:42:30,748 --> 00:42:35,586
Wasn't it you who hired Michiko Daimon?

720
00:42:36,153 --> 00:42:38,222
The patient has been infected.

721
00:42:38,289 --> 00:42:41,025
It's probably a COVID variant.

722
00:42:41,091 --> 00:42:43,160
No wonder she's operating alone.

723
00:42:43,661 --> 00:42:46,030
She doesn't want anyone else to catch it.

724
00:42:46,096 --> 00:42:47,665
Is she some kind of fool?

725
00:42:47,731 --> 00:42:49,066
She's an unbelievable fool!

726
00:42:50,200 --> 00:42:52,836
But that's the kind of doctor
Michiko Daimon is.

727
00:42:53,404 --> 00:42:56,974
Is it really all right
to let Dr. Daimon work alone?

728
00:42:58,642 --> 00:43:00,544
You call yourselves surgeons?

729
00:43:02,146 --> 00:43:03,247
Please!

730
00:43:03,314 --> 00:43:06,283
Allow us to assist
with Dr. Daimon's surgery.

731
00:43:07,585 --> 00:43:09,119
You want to do it…

732
00:43:10,154 --> 00:43:12,556
even though you know the risks involved?

733
00:43:14,258 --> 00:43:16,026
- Then do it!
- Don't you dare!

734
00:43:16,093 --> 00:43:19,129
If there's an outbreak in Surgery,
you'll all be done for!

735
00:43:19,196 --> 00:43:22,366
- You wouldn't understand!
- That's right! We are surgeons!

736
00:43:22,433 --> 00:43:25,603
We've been vaccinated. We'll be just fine!

737
00:43:25,669 --> 00:43:27,972
Let's show them what surgeons are made of!

738
00:43:28,038 --> 00:43:29,273
Let's go! See you later!

739
00:43:29,340 --> 00:43:30,908
- You're doing it?
- Let's go!

740
00:43:30,975 --> 00:43:32,876
- You're doing it? Then go.
- Yes. Thank you.

741
00:43:32,943 --> 00:43:34,311
- Counting on you.
- Right!

742
00:43:39,183 --> 00:43:44,722
I will now perform a cardiolysis
for constrictive pericarditis.

743
00:43:44,788 --> 00:43:47,524
BP 112 over 63, normal sinus rhythm.

744
00:43:49,593 --> 00:43:50,594
Get out!

745
00:43:50,661 --> 00:43:52,329
Dr. Daimon! Let us battle alongside you!

746
00:43:52,396 --> 00:43:53,430
Don't brave this alone!

747
00:43:53,497 --> 00:43:54,665
Don't come in here. Get out!

748
00:43:54,732 --> 00:43:57,835
- What? But why?
- Get out!

749
00:43:57,901 --> 00:43:58,736
Dr. Daimon!

750
00:44:00,104 --> 00:44:03,007
Dr. Ichiki's test results are back.

751
00:44:06,010 --> 00:44:07,711
I knew it. Positive.

752
00:44:09,847 --> 00:44:12,583
Dr. Daimon, stop this surgery now.

753
00:44:12,650 --> 00:44:14,485
It's insane to operate now. Stop!

754
00:44:14,551 --> 00:44:15,386
Dr. Daimon,

755
00:44:15,452 --> 00:44:17,888
we're prepared to contract
a COVID variant!

756
00:44:18,689 --> 00:44:20,057
It's not COVID!

757
00:44:21,025 --> 00:44:22,192
Then what is it?

758
00:44:25,462 --> 00:44:26,664
Lassa fever.

759
00:44:28,699 --> 00:44:30,467
Lassa fever?

760
00:44:41,245 --> 00:44:43,013
Oh, my goodness.

761
00:44:43,080 --> 00:44:44,515
Lassa fever…

762
00:44:44,581 --> 00:44:46,583
Dr. Daimon, I'm sorry.

763
00:44:47,117 --> 00:44:48,052
What?

764
00:44:48,118 --> 00:44:50,354
- He's all yours.
- What?

765
00:44:50,421 --> 00:44:51,622
Sorry.

766
00:44:52,122 --> 00:44:53,557
- Are you okay?
- I'm fine!

767
00:44:53,624 --> 00:44:54,692
Hey, wait!

768
00:44:55,259 --> 00:44:57,861
I thought we were showing them
what we're made of!

769
00:44:58,395 --> 00:44:59,430
Wait!

770
00:45:00,297 --> 00:45:01,965
Ms. Daimon!

771
00:45:02,032 --> 00:45:04,334
Damn it, Ms. Daimon! Open up!

772
00:45:04,401 --> 00:45:06,670
Ms. Daimon! Open up!

773
00:45:07,171 --> 00:45:08,272
Open this door!

774
00:45:16,246 --> 00:45:20,317
Doing heart surgery
on a patient with Lassa fever?

775
00:45:20,384 --> 00:45:21,385
This is insane!

776
00:45:22,019 --> 00:45:23,687
I'm telling you again.

777
00:45:23,754 --> 00:45:25,689
Stop this surgery!

778
00:45:26,290 --> 00:45:27,424
Dr. Daimon!

779
00:45:27,958 --> 00:45:29,293
Can't you hear us?

780
00:45:29,359 --> 00:45:33,130
There is no vaccine or remedy
for Lassa fever!

781
00:45:33,197 --> 00:45:35,199
Cases in Japan are unheard of!

782
00:45:35,265 --> 00:45:38,469
Over 20% of serious cases die!

783
00:45:38,535 --> 00:45:40,471
- Don't you understand?
- Shut up!

784
00:46:02,126 --> 00:46:03,360
Ms. Daimon…

785
00:46:19,042 --> 00:46:20,944
BP has fallen to 65.

786
00:46:21,011 --> 00:46:22,045
LOW BLOOD PRESSURE ALARM

787
00:46:25,048 --> 00:46:26,250
The aorta has ruptured.

788
00:46:30,087 --> 00:46:31,522
His aorta is hemorrhaging?

789
00:46:31,588 --> 00:46:32,723
Why?

790
00:46:33,624 --> 00:46:36,960
Ablation of the pericardium
improved the heart's contractions.

791
00:46:37,027 --> 00:46:39,329
But the aortic walls,
weakened by inflammation,

792
00:46:39,396 --> 00:46:41,498
became distorted and ruptured.

793
00:46:41,565 --> 00:46:44,768
She's working alone without even
an artificial heart-lung apparatus.

794
00:46:45,469 --> 00:46:47,437
There's no way she'll succeed.

795
00:46:48,205 --> 00:46:49,239
Ms. Daimon…

796
00:46:57,548 --> 00:46:59,516
I can't see the hemorrhage source.

797
00:47:02,119 --> 00:47:04,021
Changing surgical field.

798
00:47:19,303 --> 00:47:23,674
Each drop of blood
is incredibly contagious.

799
00:47:28,712 --> 00:47:30,013
Akira!

800
00:47:34,318 --> 00:47:36,386
Michiko, stay calm.

801
00:47:37,054 --> 00:47:39,590
Temporarily stop his heart.

802
00:47:39,656 --> 00:47:41,458
Stop his heart?

803
00:47:41,525 --> 00:47:44,294
Find the rupture and repair it.

804
00:47:48,432 --> 00:47:50,000
Injecting adenosine triphosphate.

805
00:48:14,091 --> 00:48:15,525
I have three minutes.

806
00:48:15,592 --> 00:48:18,061
Ms. Daimon, I'll keep time for you!

807
00:48:23,533 --> 00:48:24,501
Five seconds.

808
00:48:28,572 --> 00:48:29,773
Ten seconds.

809
00:49:00,570 --> 00:49:02,072
It's beating again…

810
00:49:02,139 --> 00:49:03,507
It's beating again?

811
00:49:04,574 --> 00:49:07,978
- But it hasn't been three minutes!
- She can't control it.

812
00:49:08,045 --> 00:49:09,313
Hurry, Michiko.

813
00:49:31,568 --> 00:49:32,903
Damn it!

814
00:49:33,804 --> 00:49:35,872
I can't see the suturing
due to the bleeding!

815
00:49:47,284 --> 00:49:48,251
Ms. Daimon…

816
00:50:45,642 --> 00:50:46,643
I…

817
00:50:47,177 --> 00:50:48,645
will not fail.

818
00:50:58,088 --> 00:50:59,189
There it is.

819
00:51:34,991 --> 00:51:38,562
Rupture repair complete.

820
00:51:42,399 --> 00:51:43,934
I'll close the chest.

821
00:52:01,151 --> 00:52:02,285
Done.

822
00:52:03,186 --> 00:52:06,123
BP 123 over 71, normal sinus rhythm.

823
00:52:12,829 --> 00:52:14,464
Well done.

824
00:52:17,868 --> 00:52:20,737
Thoroughly disinfect the OR.

825
00:52:20,804 --> 00:52:21,771
Yes, sir.

826
00:52:32,182 --> 00:52:33,416
Ms. Daimon,

827
00:52:34,217 --> 00:52:35,652
well done.

828
00:52:35,719 --> 00:52:36,553
Ms. Daimon!

829
00:52:36,620 --> 00:52:38,088
Good work!

830
00:52:39,055 --> 00:52:40,457
You take too many risks.

831
00:52:41,158 --> 00:52:42,359
Michiko.

832
00:52:43,727 --> 00:52:45,295
You did well.

833
00:52:49,266 --> 00:52:54,104
I will now enter quarantine!

834
00:53:01,678 --> 00:53:05,382
Dr. Hachisuka was so shocked.
He hasn't left his office.

835
00:53:05,448 --> 00:53:08,451
After seeing that awesome surgery,
he must have chickened out.

836
00:53:08,518 --> 00:53:11,154
We showed him what surgeons are made of!

837
00:53:12,522 --> 00:53:15,759
But you two didn't do a thing.

838
00:53:15,825 --> 00:53:17,694
- Yes.
- Right?

839
00:53:17,761 --> 00:53:20,830
Mr. Kambara
of Kambara Doctor Referral Agency is here.

840
00:53:20,897 --> 00:53:23,600
Well, all the doctors are here.

841
00:53:23,667 --> 00:53:24,701
Excuse me.

842
00:53:25,435 --> 00:53:30,407
Now, wait a minute.
Wasn't Dr. Michiko Daimon…

843
00:53:32,242 --> 00:53:37,180
hired by Director
of Internal Medicine Hachisuka?

844
00:53:37,247 --> 00:53:40,550
You go and see Hachisuka.

845
00:53:41,284 --> 00:53:42,719
- Well, you see…
- What?

846
00:53:42,786 --> 00:53:46,990
Director Hachisuka has toughened
COVID restrictions,

847
00:53:47,057 --> 00:53:50,860
so you can only meet with him
via video conference.

848
00:53:50,927 --> 00:53:52,395
This is a melon.

849
00:53:56,299 --> 00:53:57,467
This is the bill.

850
00:53:57,534 --> 00:53:58,668
Really?

851
00:53:59,769 --> 00:54:04,040
Considering this day and age,
it's quite reasonable.

852
00:54:06,876 --> 00:54:10,213
How can you call this reasonable?

853
00:54:10,280 --> 00:54:14,117
The surgery fees
have been drastically reduced,

854
00:54:14,184 --> 00:54:16,253
but independent surgery fees,

855
00:54:16,319 --> 00:54:20,624
COVID restriction fees,
and other fees were added.

856
00:54:22,225 --> 00:54:23,493
How many zeroes?

857
00:54:24,527 --> 00:54:27,631
One, two, three, four, five, six, seven.

858
00:54:27,697 --> 00:54:28,932
SURGICAL FEES

859
00:54:30,667 --> 00:54:33,270
Now, Mr. Kambara,

860
00:54:34,504 --> 00:54:39,376
Dr. Michiko Daimon did this
without permission.

861
00:54:39,442 --> 00:54:41,811
I can't pay this.

862
00:54:41,878 --> 00:54:44,147
Don't be like that.

863
00:54:44,914 --> 00:54:46,650
I will pay for it.

864
00:54:46,716 --> 00:54:48,485
Representative Hitotsubashi.

865
00:54:48,551 --> 00:54:52,188
She saved my life
as well as my attending physician.

866
00:54:53,556 --> 00:54:55,125
You're incredible.

867
00:54:55,191 --> 00:54:56,493
Excuse me.

868
00:54:58,461 --> 00:54:59,996
This is a melon.

869
00:55:00,063 --> 00:55:01,231
This is the bill.

870
00:55:04,134 --> 00:55:07,137
I made a bundle!

871
00:55:07,203 --> 00:55:09,172
Thank you!

872
00:55:11,207 --> 00:55:12,275
Michiko!

873
00:55:13,476 --> 00:55:14,577
Akira!

874
00:55:16,313 --> 00:55:19,249
- Did you get a test today?
- What?

875
00:55:19,316 --> 00:55:21,551
- A test!
- Yes, I did.

876
00:55:21,618 --> 00:55:23,186
But the results aren't back yet.

877
00:55:23,253 --> 00:55:26,323
Don't worry.
You won't have to wait much longer.

878
00:55:27,791 --> 00:55:30,860
Michiko. Surprise!

879
00:55:30,927 --> 00:55:32,295
They're huge!

880
00:55:32,362 --> 00:55:36,299
I had the usual <i>taiyaki</i> shop
make them special.

881
00:55:36,366 --> 00:55:40,236
They're packed with bean jam
from the head to the tail!

882
00:55:40,303 --> 00:55:42,272
You can eat them all yourself!

883
00:55:43,239 --> 00:55:46,876
Akira! I love you!

884
00:55:48,244 --> 00:55:49,179
Ouch!

885
00:55:49,245 --> 00:55:50,547
Michiko?

886
00:55:50,613 --> 00:55:53,083
Sorry. My head hurts.

887
00:55:53,650 --> 00:55:55,118
- Michiko!
- My head…

888
00:55:55,185 --> 00:55:57,153
- Ouch!
- Michiko!

889
00:55:57,220 --> 00:55:58,388
Ouch!

890
00:56:01,891 --> 00:56:03,793
- Ouch, it hurts!
- Michiko!

891
00:56:04,994 --> 00:56:06,029
Michiko!

892
00:56:10,567 --> 00:56:11,868
<i>She hates groups,</i>

893
00:56:11,935 --> 00:56:13,136
<i>she hates authorities,</i>

894
00:56:13,203 --> 00:56:14,738
<i>and she hates constraints.</i>

895
00:56:14,804 --> 00:56:17,540
<i>Her weapons are her specialty license</i>
<i>and her skill</i>

896
00:56:17,607 --> 00:56:18,775
<i> to work her way up.</i>

897
00:56:18,842 --> 00:56:21,044
Saturation under 90%!

898
00:56:21,111 --> 00:56:21,978
Michiko…

899
00:56:22,045 --> 00:56:23,880
- Demon!
- Dr. Daimon!

900
00:56:23,947 --> 00:56:25,648
Dr. Daimon, you hang in there!

901
00:56:29,052 --> 00:56:30,086
Michiko!

902
00:56:34,290 --> 00:56:38,695
I've… caught it…

903
00:56:39,295 --> 00:56:41,831
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon.</i>

904
00:56:42,332 --> 00:56:45,535
<i>Also known as… Doctor X.</i>

905
00:56:45,602 --> 00:56:48,605
Dr. Daimon, pull yourself together!

906
00:56:48,671 --> 00:56:50,173
Dr. Daimon!

907
00:57:35,852 --> 00:57:38,354
<i>We need your skills.</i>

908
00:57:38,421 --> 00:57:40,857
Could this be revenge for back then?

909
00:57:40,924 --> 00:57:42,025
You infection maniac.

910
00:57:42,091 --> 00:57:43,226
You… promotion maniac.

911
00:57:43,293 --> 00:57:44,494
I want to do surgeries!

912
00:57:44,561 --> 00:57:46,596
<i>Meeting you at a place like this,</i>

913
00:57:46,663 --> 00:57:47,664
it feels like fate.

914
00:57:47,730 --> 00:57:48,898
<i>Hitting on women in the OR.</i>

915
00:57:49,466 --> 00:57:50,300
So you're running away again.

916
00:57:50,366 --> 00:57:51,201
Subtitle translation by: Brian Athey
